				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Snide didn’t have any friends.  Most people he had tricked or deceived and they had despised him for it.  He was surprised with his acceptance into Dark Inheritance.  He started a language faire with the hope that he would become powerful, being able to spy on others.  He couldn’t believe that so many he didn’t know would come to teach him languages.  At first he wanted just to take their knowledge for himself, but something almost touched his soul then when he saw the way they gave so freely.  
<br />
	Snide tried to cut back these feelings, but they seemed to creep out.  He found himself being nice, when all he had ever been was… snide.  He felt he belonged somewhere, finally when he had lost hope of ever finding something called home.  He almost felt like Cemberfrost was a brother, someone with his racial heritage, that was friendly to him.  Most of his race thought he was a no good thief.  At least Cemberfrost believed he was thief.  Snide was almost happy, but then something terrible happened.
<br />
	Cemberfrost’s death tormented him.  He heard bits and pieces from witnesses, how Darianna from Domus Solis hit Cemberfrost with a staff and how he was set on fire, also how he fought with Deathadder and Menethel from Domus Noctis.  Snide was confused. Why had those he thought were his allies attacked one of his friends, in fact his only true friend.  He heard of a demon, and flames, consuming all of Domus Umbra’s hall.  He heard so many things and he didn’t know what to believe.
<br />
	Snide knew that his life in Domus Umbra was too good to be true.  Something always happened to make his life hell again.  He would never be happy, there would always be something tearing his life apart.  Snide refused to give up though.  He told all of Domus Umbra that he would lead, he would set everything right.  He would go to Blackburrow to build the new hall for Domus Umbra.  There no one would come to destroy them, because they would not come to so insignificant a place.
<br />
	Those of Domus Umbra thought him mad, they did not follow Snide, although they tried to persuade him to mourn for Cemberfrost and not dishonor his death, but doing foolish things.  He ignored them and dug in the earth with a pick, into the burrow, batting away the gnolls that got in his way.  It is said that Cemberfrost’s death drove him mad, and there he hides, in a cave of the Blackburrow, near madness.<br />_________________<br /><img src="http://images.deviantart.com/i/2003/36/d/3/snideripped.jpg" border="0" /></span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
