			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=1243&amp;sid=81654a0de8b1629390c40b1a1d6f2d3d#1243"><img src="templates/smartDark/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Tue Jul 29, 2003 12:08 am<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: Episode 2</span></td>
				<td valign="top" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=1243&amp;sid=81654a0de8b1629390c40b1a1d6f2d3d"><img src="templates/smartDark/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Serrik walked quickly through the entrance shaped like a gnoll's head, past the cowering dogs, to the interior of Blackburrow.  He turned his head and followed the diseased rat that walked along the ground.  It came to a short cavern on the left side of the entrance.   There sat the the rogue.  It was obvious he hadn’t bathed in quite a while.  His beard has fully grown in, and a few sticks were stuck in his natty hair.  Serrik could smell his stench from a few yards away.  
<br />

<br />
	Snide was sitting on a crude seat, ground from the rock off the wall.  He held a gnoll head in his hand, but it had probably been dead for more than a week.  Maggots had eaten most of the flesh.  Serrik sighed and began.
<br />

<br />
	"Hello Snide.”
<br />

<br />
	Snide continued to peer into the skull and then tossed it on the ground.
<br />

<br />
	“Get out of the hall of Umbra.  You are not welcome here,” he said sharply.
<br />

<br />
	“Snide you must stop this.  You are no leader of Domus Umbra.  Altus Concilium normally does not intervene in the affairs of the houses, but you have claimed leadership with no one to back you up, and none offer their support.  You are being stupid, come out of this burrow.”
<br />

<br />
	  “No one else can take the responsibility; I’m the only one left strong enough.  Hylphae has been consumed with a rage to destroy.  Destroy!  Just as Cemberfrost had been.  If only Cemberfrost was here, he was the closest thing I ever had to a brother.”
<br />

<br />
	Snide frowned and looked down at his forearms.  On his arms were golden-chain bracers that Cemberfrost had given to him.  There were covered in dirt.
<br />

<br />
	“I still don’t believe some demon killed him…”
<br />

<br />
	“Cemberfrost’s death affected us all.  Yes Hylphae is acting strangely but that’s no reason to try and take Domus Umbra into your own hands.  I encouraged them to try to reason with you, but it seems like you will listen to no one,”  Serrik shook his head.
<br />

<br />
	“Domus Umbra is weak without Cemberfrost and Hylphae to protect it.  I must be strong for everyone else even if they don’t like it.”
<br />

<br />
	“I need you to come out of here for your own good, no one is paying attention to you and besides, dictatorship is not what the house of neutrals honors.”
<br />

<br />
	“Things change,” Snide said flatly.  “The other houses are trying to take advantage of us.  Menethel, that bitch, was behind his death.  Dariana too, his so-called love.  I heard she lit him on fire with a torch.” Snide began to raise his  voice.  “The ‘good’ and ‘evil’ houses have combined to destroy us!  Hylphae turned away, and now continues his destruction of everything.  We have traitors and if I don’t protect us, no one will!”  Snide began to yell.
<br />

<br />
	“Never!” Serrik said very loudly.  Snide was silienced.  “Never call anyone of our guild a traitor unless you have proof.  Your exaggerating Snide,” Serrik said with a solumn stare.  “Altus Concilium will protect your house if needed, but your ideas are wild.  I can see where you might think the houses may be out for you, but it is not so.  We have a truce here in the Dark Inheritance.”
<br />

<br />
	“Your lying,” Snide clenched his teeth, “They want to destroy us.”  Snide drew his hook from the back of his belt and pointed it forward at Serrik.
<br />

<br />
	Serrik calmly raised his hands.
<br />
	“Calm down, don’t make this harder than it has to be.”
<br />

<br />
	“Altus Concilium is against us as well? Aren’t you?  I’m the only one that is willing to protect us!”
<br />

<br />
	“Snide you obviously aren’t stable enough to even realize what is happening.  Your not the leader of Domus Umbra, you’ve been hiding here for too long, not knowing what is happening in the real world.  I will forcibly remove you from this burrow till you regain your senses if I must.”
<br />

<br />
	“Not likely,” Snide backed up into the shadows and Serrik calmly watched as the rogue disappeared.  Serrik turned his back to where Snide once was and closed his eyes.
<br />
	Then he moved suddenly to the right and spun on his heel.  Snide appeared, stabbing his hook forward to where Serrik once was standing.  Serrik drove a roundhouse kick into Snide’s back, flinging him against the wall, as the rogue’s hook clattered to the ground.
<br />

<br />
	“Poor fool,” Serrik said, shaking his head.  “I do hope that knocked some sense into you.”<br />_________________<br /><img src="http://images.deviantart.com/i/2003/36/d/3/snideripped.jpg" border="0" /></span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
