				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Episode 3
<br />

<br />
	Snide woke up with a terrible headache.  His vision was a little blurred.  He rolled onto his side and opened his eyes.  Raiya was standing over him, in the night air of Shadowhaven, in the hall of Altus Concilium.  He lay on the floor, a bruise on the side of his head.
<br />

<br />
	“Finally decided to wake up?” she said with a smile.
<br />

<br />
	“Where is Serrik” Snide groaned.
<br />

<br />
	“I’m here,” Serrik said from behind.  Serrik stood with his arms folded in front of himself.  
<br />

<br />
	“Snide, Cemberfrost has come back.  He came soon after Serrik went to get you.  He is the leader of Domus Umbra.”
<br />

<br />
	“What? Impossible!  I saw his body.  Is this another trick,” Snide turned around to look at Serrik.
<br />

<br />
	“Calm down.  This is no trick,” Cemberfrost said as he walked through the door.  His hair was still as red as ever, and his eyes were blue, but they did not flame as they used to.
<br />

<br />
	Snide coughed and sat up wide eyed, folding his legs in front of himself.
<br />

<br />
	“I know I was foolish to try and lead Domus Umbra, I’m no leader.  I’ll leave Dark Inheritance, I have no place here,” he said with a frown.
<br />

<br />
	“Don’t be hasty,” Cemberfost said. 
<br />

<br />
	Raiya spoke again, “You’re welcome to stay in Dark Inheritance despite what problems you had.”
<br />

<br />
	“You need to stop jumping to conclusions,” Serrik said sharply.  “Everything is fine now.”
<br />

<br />
	“No, I realize now that I don’t belong here.  I tried to fool myself into believing I could make friends.  At first it was an experiment for me, trying to get powerful allies, but then I was tempted into making true friends.  I see that I was wrong.  All these people show friendship for me when they know nothing about me.  I deserve none of their kindness and only their ire.  You can have your friendship; your lives are filled with hollow pursuit of it.  I am giving it up, because it never can be obtained.  I can make it on my own.”
<br />

<br />
	Snide picked up his hook and hobbled to his feet. He strode towards the door.  Cemberfrost caught his arm and Snide looked back.  Snide's eyes had clouded over with apathy.  Cemberfrost sighed in disapointment and let him go.
<br />

<br />
                "Good luck friend," Cemberfrost said.
<br />

<br />
                "Keep your luck.  I have my own."
<br />

<br />
                Snide walked into the streets of Shadowhaven.  Altus Concilium and Domus Umbra looked on him as he left, knowing he did so of his free will, and knowing that they had no right to stop him, even though he left for the wrong reasons.
<br />

<br />
/ooc *Note from the author*:  sorry to cut and run, but Snide is happier belonging to no guild or house.  I’m keen to group with you guys, but to be honest I can’t RP snide in a guild, he’s supposed to be mean, and friendless and I haven’t been playing him that way, for fear of hurting peoples feelings in the guild.  I've been thinking more about his character while I've been gone from EQ.  It will make Snide more happy, even though I love you guys <img src="images/smiles/icon_sad.gif" alt="icon_sad.gif" border="0" />
<br />
Send me a private message if anyone wants to talk about it.
<br />
Ryan<br />_________________<br /><img src="http://images.deviantart.com/i/2003/36/d/3/snideripped.jpg" border="0" /></span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
