				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=1452&amp;sid=81654a0de8b1629390c40b1a1d6f2d3d#1452"><img src="templates/smartDark/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Sun Sep 07, 2003 1:27 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: Episode 4</span></td>
				<td valign="top" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=1452&amp;sid=81654a0de8b1629390c40b1a1d6f2d3d"><img src="templates/smartDark/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Snide pressed his hands against the Book of Knowledge in the Nexus and felt the surge of energy enter his body.  From the Plane of Knowledge he traveled to Freeport, City of Men.  Snide felt he needed to be back on Norrath.  He never liked the moon much anyway.  All sorts of strange aliens and huge cats made it too strange a place for his liking.  Snide covered his face with his burnoose of the half-breed, transforming his image into a short but handsome half-elf and walked through the streets until he arrived at the tavern at the docks.  He entered with a smile, ready to drown his foolishness in drink.
<br />

<br />
	After becoming very drunk he passed out on the dock, the tavern had kicked him out because he had run out of money and he was barely able to walk.  His illusion faded as the night wore on.  An owl howled from far off.
<br />

<br />
	A fell wind blew across the east coast of Antonica bringing dark sails to Freeport.  Beneath a black flag, trolls and men dredged the port for wealth and those to shanghai.  A burly troll picked up the unconscious rogue and walked down the pier with him.  As he got to the ship he tossed him onto the main deck. 
<br />
 
<br />
	“Another sailor for youse Cap’n,” the troll said with a smile.
<br />

<br />
	The fog filtered across the deck to reveal the captain of the StormWave, an iksar.  He wore a cap made from a Vah Shir’s skull.  Most of the Broken skull pirates were branded or tattooed with a Broken Skull insignia, but iksar scales couldn’t be marked in the same way.  The tattoos were to mark people as property of Innoruuk, but they basically served as incentive for the sailors to not dissert.  Anyone on land knows that pirates are the vilest of scum and should be hanged for their many crimes.  There was not much reason to try to find a way to mark iksar though, since most everyone hated them anyway.	
<br />

<br />
	“Exssellent.  Go join the others,” the iksar said.  The troll ran off to rape and pillage with the other pirates.  
<br />

<br />
	The iksar’s chest was covered with a loose fitting shirt that was open at the front and a silver ring went through his snout.  A red sash covered his waist.  Over his legs he wore small sheets of fine plate that had been oxidized by the sea water and air.  They looked rather rusty.  He walked down the ramp to the pier, using his barnacle covered truncheon as a walking staff.  He turned to look back at the barbarian on the deck.  There was a leather thong across his face that held an emerald crystal in place of his left eye.  Captain Osaftars smirked as the screams from Freeport reached his ears.  He would have fun trying to break the first barbarian to the ways of the pirate.
<br />

<br />
